{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\fs24\b\fs32 VITL Project Brief\b0\fs24\parInternal working brief\par\par\b Project Summary\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab VITL is evolving from a simple conversational prototype into a structured simulation product with scenario logic, learner assessment, and structured documentation flows.\par\tab\bullet\tab The active case is a pediatric infant UTI encounter focused on communication with the infant's mother.\par\par\b What Matters Right Now\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab Simulation-aware routing between MetaDynVoiceController and VITLSimulationManager is a central part of the current design.\par\tab\bullet\tab Model-backed communication scoring through OpenRouter is the intended primary scoring path, with fallback scoring preserved for resilience.\par\tab\bullet\tab Activity 2 should capture learner-entered patient history as structured runtime data rather than inferred LLM extraction.\par\par\b Milestone 1 Scope\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab Greeting / rapport flow.\par\tab\bullet\tab Threshold-based activity progression.\par\tab\bullet\tab Simulation-aware mother response after scoring.\par\tab\bullet\tab Structured history intake as a distinct Activity 2 flow.\par\tab\bullet\tab Analytics-safe milestone events where useful.\par\par\b Out of Scope\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab Full automated clinical grading.\par\tab\bullet\tab Automatic extraction of structured history from mother dialogue.\par\tab\bullet\tab Complete reporting/export stack.\par\tab\bullet\tab Large-scale rewrite of string-based event surfaces.\par\par\b Operational Read\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab The strongest architectural line in the current VITL material is separation of concerns: conversation history, learner scoring, simulation state, and patient-history documentation should remain distinct layers with clear ownership.\par\tab\bullet\tab That separation should stay intact as implementation moves forward.\par\par}